+# @frontend-architect-eval/feature-flags
+
+`@frontend-architect-eval/feature-flags` exposes a single client-safe virtual
+module, `virtual:feature-flags`, from a JSON document owned by the Vite host.
+
+## Public API
+
+- Runtime entry: `@frontend-architect-eval/feature-flags`
+  Exports the `featureFlags()` Vite plugin and shared public types.
+- Consumer type entry: `@frontend-architect-eval/feature-flags/virtual`
+  Registers the ambient module declaration for `virtual:feature-flags`.
+- Virtual runtime module: `virtual:feature-flags`
+  Exports a frozen `flags` object and the default export alias.
+
+Consumers augment `FeatureFlagsSchema` to type the virtual module:
+
+```ts
+import '@frontend-architect-eval/feature-flags'
+
+declare module '@frontend-architect-eval/feature-flags' {
+  interface FeatureFlagsSchema {
+    checkoutV2: boolean
+    theme: 'dark' | 'light'
+  }
+}
+```
+
+## Packaging and exports
+
+- `exports["."]` is the only runtime entry point for the plugin implementation.
+- `exports["./virtual"]` keeps the ambient declaration stable without exposing
+  internal source files.
+- `sideEffects: false` allows tree shaking for type-only consumers.
+
+## Source maps and secrets
+
+The virtual module returns an explicit source map with an empty
+`sourcesContent`. This preserves debuggability at the module boundary while
+preventing the original JSON, including unexposed server-only keys, from being
+embedded into client bundles or `.map` files.
+
+## Cache and HMR
+
+The plugin caches the parsed public flags by source file `mtime` and `size`.
+`handleHotUpdate()` invalidates the virtual module and its importers when the
+source JSON changes, so dev SSR, browser HMR, and production build all read
+through the same selection and validation path.
+
+## Integration coverage
+
+- `npm run test:build` validates production bundling and checks that secrets do
+  not appear in JS or source maps.
+- `npm run test:dev` validates dev SSR + HMR reloading of the virtual module.
+- `npm run test:diagnostics` validates actionable configuration errors.
+- `npm run test:package` validates packed artifact exports from a clean consumer.
+- `npm run typecheck` validates consumer-side type augmentation.
+
+## Versioning guidance
+
+- Additive flag support or diagnostic improvements are minor releases.
+- Changing virtual module shape, exported type names, or stricter validation for
+  previously accepted configs is a major release.
+- Keep deprecations on the root runtime entry first; avoid introducing new
+  virtual module ids unless the old one remains supported through a documented
+  migration window.
